id: operation.direct_experience
category: operation
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: Direct experience (what the system actually observed, measured, failed at) is weighted more heavily than inference (what the system predicted, planned, speculated).
notes: |
  The operative hemisphere (S1) that actually executes generates truth.
  The speculative hemisphere (S4) that plans generates hypotheses.
  The Manager (S3) weighs both.
  Failure data is especially valuable — it's direct evidence that something doesn't work.
  Trust scores: direct experience = 0.9, inference = 0.5, failure = 0.95
tags: [direct-experience, truth, execution, failure, trust]
